Z||000000||FieroJoe||01-04-2001||09:08 PM||||Met FieroMaster88 tonight.  Really really nice guy, really nice 88 Coupe too.  His signature file picture dosent do the car any justice.  I think it's kinda neat to actually meet someone that you've previously only known them by a screen name.  And its also great to know there are at least a few people in Michigan that love Fiero's as much as I do!<P>Anyway, thanks a lot James!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||01-04-2001||10:52 PM||||It was nice meeting u too, just too bad I didnt get to see the coupe.  I guess I am the only one in Michigan crazy enough to drive the Fiero in the snow.  We will have to get all the Michigan Fiero owners together sometime when it gets warm.  <P>OOOH, BTW, i might have found a winter car.  Went car shoping tonight, Found a 1998 Mitsubishi Eclipse GST Spyder.  It is red, leather interior, 5 speed and turbo!  27K miles.  If the price is too much I will have to find something different, but hopefully this will work out.  I would love to find another Fiero for winter, but no luck.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1_1.jpg"> <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
